WEBVTT

00:15:29.257 --> 00:15:32.090
from Diego Rodriguez,
who used to be at IDEO,

00:15:32.114 --> 00:15:33.915
and said, instead of culture fit,

00:15:33.939 --> 00:15:36.702
we should think about culture add
or culture contribution,

00:15:36.726 --> 00:15:38.138
and you should ask,

00:15:38.162 --> 00:15:40.377
'Well, what's missing from our culture

00:15:40.401 --> 00:15:41.908
and are they going to enrich it

00:15:41.932 --> 00:15:43.750
by bringing something that's absent?'"

00:15:43.774 --> 00:15:45.853
What do you think of that
as an alternative?

00:15:45.877 --> 00:15:47.551
LR: I think it's a great start.

00:15:47.575 --> 00:15:50.346
People have to actually
have a sense and have a discussion

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:53.448
about what is actually important
to us, in terms of values.

00:15:53.472 --> 00:15:56.441
(Music)

00:15:56.465 --> 00:15:58.124
AG: Identifying your team's values

00:15:58.148 --> 00:15:59.591
and your organization's values

00:15:59.615 --> 00:16:01.821
can help you focus
on the kinds of similarities